DusdPegOracleCurve::getPrice()
├── given ma_last_time reverts
│   └── it should bubble the pool revert
├── given ma_last_time returns packed timestamps
│   ├── when the low 128 bits are zero
│   │   ├── it should return priceWad as zero
│   │   ├── it should return observedAt as zero
│   │   ├── it should return valid as false
│   │   └── it should not perform runtime configuration or price reads
│   ├── when the low 128 bits are non-zero and greater than block.timestamp
│   │   ├── it should return priceWad as zero
│   │   ├── it should return observedAt as zero
│   │   ├── it should return valid as false
│   │   └── it should not perform runtime configuration or price reads
│   ├── when block.timestamp is greater than type(uint48).max and the low 128 bits are not in the future but exceed type(uint48).max
│   │   ├── it should return priceWad as zero
│   │   ├── it should return observedAt as zero
│   │   ├── it should return valid as false
│   │   └── it should not perform runtime configuration or price reads
│   ├── when the low 128 bits equal block.timestamp and fit uint48
│   │   └── it should treat the timestamp as valid
│   ├── when the low 128 bits equal type(uint48).max and are not in the future
│   │   └── it should treat the timestamp as valid
│   ├── when the low 128 bits contain an arbitrarily old non-zero timestamp
│   │   └── it should not apply a freshness check
│   └── when the high 128 bits differ while the low 128 bits are unchanged
│       └── it should return the same observedAt and validity result
├── given the observation timestamp is valid
│   ├── when ma_exp_time reverts
│   │   └── it should bubble the pool revert
│   ├── when ma_exp_time differs from expectedMaExpTime
│   │   ├── it should return priceWad as zero
│   │   ├── it should preserve the decoded observedAt
│   │   ├── it should return valid as false
│   │   └── it should not query A_precise, future_A or price_oracle
│   ├── when ma_exp_time matches and A_precise reverts
│   │   └── it should bubble the pool revert
│   ├── when ma_exp_time matches and A_precise differs from expectedAPrecise
│   │   ├── it should return priceWad as zero
│   │   ├── it should preserve the decoded observedAt
│   │   ├── it should return valid as false
│   │   └── it should not query future_A or price_oracle
│   ├── when ma_exp_time and A_precise match and future_A reverts
│   │   └── it should bubble the pool revert
│   ├── when ma_exp_time and A_precise match and future_A differs from expectedAPrecise
│   │   ├── it should return priceWad as zero
│   │   ├── it should preserve the decoded observedAt
│   │   ├── it should return valid as false
│   │   └── it should not query price_oracle
│   └── when ma_exp_time, A_precise and future_A match their approved values
│       └── it should proceed to price_oracle
├── given execution reaches the price read
│   ├── when price_oracle(0) reverts
│   │   └── it should bubble the pool revert
│   ├── when price_oracle(0) returns zero
│   │   ├── it should return priceWad as zero
│   │   ├── it should preserve the decoded observedAt
│   │   └── it should return valid as false
│   ├── when price_oracle(0) returns a non-zero price below the peg
│   │   ├── it should return the exact price
│   │   ├── it should preserve the decoded observedAt
│   │   └── it should return valid as true
│   ├── when price_oracle(0) returns type(uint256).max
│   │   ├── it should return type(uint256).max as priceWad
│   │   ├── it should preserve the decoded observedAt
│   │   └── it should return valid as true
│   └── it should query price_oracle with ORACLE_INDEX
└── given any non-reverting execution path
    ├── it should not modify contract state
    └── it should not emit events
